IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 29/6/2026 to 20/10/2026" (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (2) -- ss 243 to 248: contents of a prospectus and of a profile statement, over-subscriptions, exemptions. LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- Reading a result (the rule of 2026-10-29): JUST TRUE is yes; JUST FALSE is "the TEXT says no in its own words"; NOTHING is "the text does not say".
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Every "no" branch carries `-- FALSE-kind (...)`, every "not covered" branch `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.
-- What "investors and their professional advisers would reasonably require", what "false or misleading" means, what "unduly burdensome" means, are INPUTS (a judgment the person states).
-- "Prescribed by the Authority" and "specified by regulations" are INPUTS (a fact or a number). "Controlled by" (the person making the offer and its related parties) is one INPUT, as in section 240(4A).

-- inert (reason 1), lines 39811-39811: s 243 marginal heading: not operative.
-- repealed or blank in this text, lines 40062-40062: s 244: "[Repealed by Act 16 of 2003]".
-- inert (reason 1), lines 40064-40065: s 245 marginal heading: not operative.
-- inert (reason 1), lines 40106-40106: s 246 marginal heading: not operative.
-- inert (reason 1), lines 40168-40169: s 247 marginal heading: not operative.
-- repealed or blank in this text, lines 40193-40193: s 247(4): "[Deleted by Act 16 of 2003]".
-- inert (reason 1), lines 40206-40208: s 248 marginal heading: not operative.

§ `s 243(1) to (2): what a prospectus must contain`

DECLARE `s 243 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 245(1) accept or retain subscriptions in excess of the amount of the issue`
    `s 245(2) make, authorise or permit a statement of the asset-backing`
    `s 247(5) contravene the condition or restriction`

-- s 243(1): the prospectus contains the information and the prescribed matters. The information is "all the information that investors ... would reasonably require", as subsection (2) limits it: one fact the person states.
-- src:39813 | 243.—(1) A prospectus for an offer of securities or securities‑based
-- src:39814 | derivatives contracts must contain —
-- src:39816 | (a) all the information that investors and their professional
-- src:39817 | advisers would reasonably require to make an informed
-- src:39818 | assessment of the matters specified in subsection (3); and
-- src:39820 | (b) the matters prescribed by the Authority.
@ref s 243(1) (src:39813-39820)
GIVEN
    `the document is a prospectus for an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a prospectus for an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `it contains all the information that investors and their professional advisers would reasonably require to make an informed assessment of the matters specified in subsection (3), as subsection (2) limits it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus contain all the information that investors and their professional advisers would reasonably require to make an informed assessment of the matters in section 243(3), to the extent section 243(2) requires it?
    `it contains the matters prescribed by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus contain the matters the Authority has prescribed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(1) the prospectus contains what it must contain` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the document is a prospectus for an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A prospectus for an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts must contain"
        IF `it contains all the information that investors and their professional advisers would reasonably require to make an informed assessment of the matters specified in subsection (3), as subsection (2) limits it` AND `it contains the matters prescribed by the Authority`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must contain (a) all the information that investors and their professional advisers would reasonably require to make an informed assessment of the matters specified in subsection (3); and (b) the matters prescribed by the Authority"

-- s 243(2): an item of information the prospectus must contain. "only to the extent" closes the list.
-- src:39824 | (2) The prospectus must, with respect to subsection (1)(a), contain
-- src:39825 | such information —
-- src:39827 | (a) only to the extent to which it is reasonable for investors and
-- src:39828 | their professional advisers to expect to find in the
-- src:39829 | prospectus; and
-- src:39831 | (b) only to the extent that a person whose knowledge is
-- src:39832 | relevant —
-- src:39834 | (i) actually knows the information; or
-- src:39836 | (ii) in the circumstances ought reasonably to have
-- src:39837 | obtained the information by making enquiries.
@ref s 243(2) (src:39824-39837)
GIVEN
    `the item is information that investors and their professional advisers would reasonably require to make an informed assessment of the matters specified in subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the item information that investors and their professional advisers would reasonably require to make an informed assessment of the matters in section 243(3)?
    `it is reasonable for investors and their professional advisers to expect to find it in the prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it reasonable for investors and their professional advisers to expect to find the item in the prospectus?
    `a person whose knowledge is relevant actually knows it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a person whose knowledge is relevant (section 243(5)) actually know the item of information?
    `a person whose knowledge is relevant ought reasonably to have obtained it by making enquiries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the circumstances, ought a person whose knowledge is relevant (section 243(5)) reasonably to have obtained the item of information by making enquiries?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(2) the item of information must be contained in the prospectus` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the item is information that investors and their professional advisers would reasonably require to make an informed assessment of the matters specified in subsection (3)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The prospectus must, with respect to subsection (1)(a), contain such information"
        IF `it is reasonable for investors and their professional advisers to expect to find it in the prospectus` AND (`a person whose knowledge is relevant actually knows it` OR `a person whose knowledge is relevant ought reasonably to have obtained it by making enquiries`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, with respect to subsection (1)(a), contain such information (a) only to the extent to which it is reasonable for investors and their professional advisers to expect to find in the prospectus; and (b) only to the extent that a person whose knowledge is relevant (i) actually knows the information; or (ii) in the circumstances ought reasonably to have obtained the information by making enquiries"

§ `s 243(3): the matters the information relates to`

-- s 243(3)(a): the rights and liabilities attaching to the securities or contracts.
-- src:39839 | (3) The matters referred to in subsection (1)(a) relate to —
-- src:39841 | (a) the rights and liabilities attaching to the securities or
-- src:39842 | securities‑based derivatives contracts;
@ref s 243(3)(a) (src:39839-39842)
GIVEN
    `the matter is the rights and liabilities attaching to the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter the rights and liabilities attaching to the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(3)(a) the rights and liabilities attaching to the securities or contracts are a matter the information must relate to` MEANS
    IF `the matter is the rights and liabilities attaching to the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The matters referred to in subsection (1)(a) relate to" a list that does not end with "only"

-- s 243(3)(b): the issuer's financials, in an offer other than of units or derivatives of units in a business trust.
-- src:39844 | (b) in the case of an offer of securities or securities‑based
-- src:39845 | derivatives contracts other than units or derivatives of units
-- src:39846 | in a business trust, the assets and liabilities, profits and
-- src:39847 | losses, financial position and performance, and prospects
-- src:39848 | of the issuer;
@ref s 243(3)(b) (src:39844-39848)
GIVEN
    `the offer is of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts other than units or derivatives of units in a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts other than units or derivatives of units in a business trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(3)(b) the issuer's assets and liabilities, profits and losses, financial position and performance, and prospects are a matter the information must relate to` MEANS
    IF `the offer is of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts other than units or derivatives of units in a business trust`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) in the case of an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts other than units or derivatives of units in a business trust"

-- s 243(3)(c): the underlying entity's financials, if it is controlled by the person making the offer or its related parties. The rendering prints (c) twice, first the condition and then the matter.
-- src:39853 | (c) if the underlying entity is controlled by —
-- src:39855 | (i) the person making the offer;
-- src:39857 | (ii) one or more of the related parties of the person
-- src:39858 | making the offer; or
-- src:39860 | (iii) the person making the offer and one or more of that
-- src:39861 | person’s related parties,
-- src:39863 | (c) the assets and liabilities, profits and losses, financial
-- src:39864 | position and performance, and prospects of that entity;
@ref s 243(3)(c) (src:39853-39864)
GIVEN
    `the underlying entity is controlled by the person making the offer, by one or more of its related parties, or by that person and one or more of its related parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the underlying entity controlled by the person making the offer, by one or more of that person's related parties, or by that person and one or more of its related parties?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(3)(c) the underlying entity's assets and liabilities, profits and losses, financial position and performance, and prospects are a matter the information must relate to` MEANS
    IF `the underlying entity is controlled by the person making the offer, by one or more of its related parties, or by that person and one or more of its related parties`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(c) if the underlying entity is controlled by (i) the person making the offer; (ii) one or more of the related parties of the person making the offer; or (iii) the person making the offer and one or more of that person's related parties"

-- s 243(3)(d): the capacity to issue or deliver, in an offer of units of shares or debentures.
-- src:39866 | (d) in the case of an offer of units of shares or debentures,
-- src:39867 | where —
-- src:39869 | (i) the person making the offer is or will be required to
-- src:39870 | issue or deliver the relevant units, or meet financial
-- src:39871 | or contractual obligations to the holders of those
-- src:39872 | units; or
-- src:39874 | (ii) an entity which is controlled by one of the following
-- src:39875 | is or will be required to issue or deliver the relevant
-- src:39876 | units, or meet financial or contractual obligations to
-- src:39877 | the holders of those units:
-- src:39879 | (A) the person making the offer;
-- src:39881 | (B) one or more of the related parties of the person
-- src:39882 | making the offer;
-- src:39884 | (C) the person making the offer and one or more of
-- src:39885 | that person’s related parties,
-- src:39887 | (d) the capacity of that person or entity to issue or deliver the
-- src:39888 | relevant securities, or the ability of that person or entity to
-- src:39889 | meet those financial or contractual obligations;
@ref s 243(3)(d) (src:39866-39889)
GIVEN
    `the offer is of units of shares or debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of units of shares or debentures?
    `the person making the offer is or will be required to issue or deliver the relevant units, or meet financial or contractual obligations to the holders of those units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, as the person making the offer, or will you be, required to issue or deliver the relevant units, or to meet financial or contractual obligations to the holders of those units?
    `an entity controlled by the person making the offer, by one or more of its related parties, or by that person and one or more of its related parties is or will be required to issue or deliver the relevant units, or meet financial or contractual obligations to the holders of those units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an entity controlled by you, by one or more of your related parties, or by you and one or more of your related parties, or will it be, required to issue or deliver the relevant units, or to meet financial or contractual obligations to the holders of those units?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(3)(d) the capacity of the person or entity to issue or deliver the units, or to meet its obligations, is a matter the information must relate to` MEANS
    IF `the offer is of units of shares or debentures` AND (`the person making the offer is or will be required to issue or deliver the relevant units, or meet financial or contractual obligations to the holders of those units` OR `an entity controlled by the person making the offer, by one or more of its related parties, or by that person and one or more of its related parties is or will be required to issue or deliver the relevant units, or meet financial or contractual obligations to the holders of those units`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(d) in the case of an offer of units of shares or debentures, where (i) the person making the offer is or will be required to issue or deliver the relevant units, or meet financial or contractual obligations to the holders of those units; or (ii) an entity which is controlled by one of the following is or will be required"

-- s 243(3)(e): the business trust's and the trustee-manager's financials.
-- src:39891 | (e) in the case of an offer of securities or securities‑based
-- src:39892 | derivatives contracts being units or derivatives of units in a
-- src:39893 | business trust, where —
-- src:39895 | (i) the person making the offer is the trustee‑manager of
-- src:39896 | the business trust; or
-- src:39901 | (ii) the trustee‑manager of the business trust is controlled
-- src:39902 | by —
-- src:39904 | (A) the person making the offer;
-- src:39906 | (B) one or more of the related parties of the person
-- src:39907 | making the offer; or
-- src:39909 | (C) the person making the offer and one or more of
-- src:39910 | that person’s related parties,
-- src:39912 | (e) the assets and liabilities, profits and losses, financial
-- src:39913 | position and performance of the business trust and of the
-- src:39914 | trustee‑manager, and the prospects of the business trust;
@ref s 243(3)(e) (src:39891-39914)
GIVEN
    `the offer is of units or derivatives of units in a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of units or derivatives of units in a business trust?
    `the person making the offer is the trustee-manager of the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, as the person making the offer, the trustee-manager of the business trust?
    `the trustee-manager of the business trust is controlled by the person making the offer, by one or more of its related parties, or by that person and one or more of its related parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trustee-manager of the business trust controlled by you, by one or more of your related parties, or by you and one or more of your related parties?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(3)(e) the business trust's and the trustee-manager's assets and liabilities, profits and losses, financial position and performance, and the prospects of the business trust, are a matter the information must relate to` MEANS
    IF `the offer is of units or derivatives of units in a business trust` AND (`the person making the offer is the trustee-manager of the business trust` OR `the trustee-manager of the business trust is controlled by the person making the offer, by one or more of its related parties, or by that person and one or more of its related parties`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(e) in the case of an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts being units or derivatives of units in a business trust, where (i) the person making the offer is the trustee-manager of the business trust; or (ii) the trustee-manager of the business trust is controlled by"

-- s 243(3)(f): the financials of the entity A that issues derivatives of units in a business trust, where A is not the trustee-manager. The rendering prints (f) twice.
-- src:39916 | (f) in the case of an offer of securities or securities‑based
-- src:39917 | derivatives contracts being derivatives of units in a
-- src:39918 | business trust issued by an entity (A) other than the
-- src:39919 | trustee‑manager of the business trust, where —
-- src:39921 | (i) the person making the offer is A; or
-- src:39923 | (ii) A is controlled by —
-- src:39925 | (A) the person making the offer;
-- src:39927 | (B) one or more of the related parties of the person
-- src:39928 | making the offer; or
-- src:39930 | (C) the person making the offer and one or more of
-- src:39931 | that person’s related parties,
-- src:39933 | (f) the assets and liabilities, profits and losses, financial
-- src:39934 | position and performance, and prospects of A; and
@ref s 243(3)(f) (src:39916-39934)
GIVEN
    `the offer is of derivatives of units in a business trust issued by an entity other than the trustee-manager of the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of derivatives of units in a business trust issued by an entity (call it A) other than the trustee-manager of the business trust?
    `the person making the offer is A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, as the person making the offer, the entity that issues the derivatives?
    `A is controlled by the person making the offer, by one or more of its related parties, or by that person and one or more of its related parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity that issues the derivatives controlled by you, by one or more of your related parties, or by you and one or more of your related parties?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(3)(f) the assets and liabilities, profits and losses, financial position and performance, and prospects of the issuing entity are a matter the information must relate to` MEANS
    IF `the offer is of derivatives of units in a business trust issued by an entity other than the trustee-manager of the business trust` AND (`the person making the offer is A` OR `A is controlled by the person making the offer, by one or more of its related parties, or by that person and one or more of its related parties`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(f) in the case of an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts being derivatives of units in a business trust issued by an entity (A) other than the trustee-manager of the business trust, where (i) the person making the offer is A; or (ii) A is controlled by"

-- s 243(3)(g): the capacity to issue or deliver the units or derivatives of units, in an offer of derivatives of units in the business trust.
-- src:39936 | (g) in the case of an offer of securities or securities‑based
-- src:39937 | derivatives contracts being derivatives of units in the
-- src:39938 | business trust, where —
-- src:39940 | (i) the person making the offer is or will be required to
-- src:39941 | issue or deliver the relevant units or derivatives of
-- src:39942 | units, or meet financial or contractual obligations to
-- src:39943 | the holders of those derivatives of units; or
-- src:39945 | (ii) an entity which is controlled by one of the following
-- src:39946 | is or will be required to issue or deliver the relevant
-- src:39951 | units or derivatives of units, or meet financial or
-- src:39952 | contractual obligations to the holders of those
-- src:39953 | derivatives of units:
-- src:39955 | (A) the person making the offer;
-- src:39957 | (B) one or more of the related parties of the person
-- src:39958 | making the offer;
-- src:39960 | (C) the person making the offer and one or more of
-- src:39961 | that person’s related parties,
-- src:39963 | (g) the capacity of that person or entity to issue or deliver the
-- src:39964 | relevant units or derivatives of units in that business trust,
-- src:39965 | or the ability of that person or entity to meet those financial
-- src:39966 | or contractual obligations.
@ref s 243(3)(g) (src:39936-39966)
GIVEN
    `the offer is of derivatives of units in the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of derivatives of units in the business trust?
    `the person making the offer is or will be required to issue or deliver the relevant units or derivatives of units, or meet financial or contractual obligations to the holders of those derivatives of units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you, as the person making the offer, or will you be, required to issue or deliver the relevant units or derivatives of units, or to meet financial or contractual obligations to the holders of those derivatives of units?
    `an entity controlled by the person making the offer, by one or more of its related parties, or by that person and one or more of its related parties is or will be required to issue or deliver the relevant units or derivatives of units, or meet financial or contractual obligations to the holders of those derivatives of units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an entity controlled by you, by one or more of your related parties, or by you and one or more of your related parties, or will it be, required to issue or deliver the relevant units or derivatives of units, or to meet financial or contractual obligations to the holders of those derivatives of units?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(3)(g) the capacity of the person or entity to issue or deliver the units or derivatives of units, or to meet its obligations, is a matter the information must relate to` MEANS
    IF `the offer is of derivatives of units in the business trust` AND (`the person making the offer is or will be required to issue or deliver the relevant units or derivatives of units, or meet financial or contractual obligations to the holders of those derivatives of units` OR `an entity controlled by the person making the offer, by one or more of its related parties, or by that person and one or more of its related parties is or will be required to issue or deliver the relevant units or derivatives of units, or meet financial or contractual obligations to the holders of those derivatives of units`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(g) in the case of an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts being derivatives of units in the business trust, where (i) the person making the offer is or will be required to issue or deliver the relevant units or derivatives of units, or meet financial or contractual obligations to the holders of those derivatives of units; or (ii) an entity which is controlled by one of the following is or will be required"

§ `s 243(4) to (8): regard, incorporation by reference, relevant knowledge, waivers and definitions`

-- s 243(4): in deciding what information must be included, regard must be had to three things.
-- src:39970 | (4) In deciding what information must be included under
-- src:39971 | subsection (1)(a), regard must be had to —
-- src:39973 | (a) the nature of the securities or securities‑based derivatives
-- src:39974 | contracts and the nature of the entity concerned;
-- src:39976 | (b) the matters that likely investors may reasonably be
-- src:39977 | expected to know; and
-- src:39979 | (c) the fact that certain matters may reasonably be expected to
-- src:39980 | be known to the professional advisers of such investors.
@ref s 243(4) (src:39970-39980)
GIVEN
    `a decision is made about what information must be included under subsection (1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a decision being made about what information must be included in the prospectus under section 243(1)(a)?
    `regard has been had to the nature of the securities or contracts and the nature of the entity concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has regard been had to the nature of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts and the nature of the entity concerned?
    `regard has been had to the matters that likely investors may reasonably be expected to know` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has regard been had to the matters that likely investors may reasonably be expected to know?
    `regard has been had to the fact that certain matters may reasonably be expected to be known to the professional advisers of such investors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has regard been had to the fact that certain matters may reasonably be expected to be known to the professional advisers of such investors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(4) regard has been had to the matters` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `a decision is made about what information must be included under subsection (1)(a)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In deciding what information must be included under subsection (1)(a), regard must be had to"
        IF `regard has been had to the nature of the securities or contracts and the nature of the entity concerned` AND `regard has been had to the matters that likely investors may reasonably be expected to know` AND `regard has been had to the fact that certain matters may reasonably be expected to be known to the professional advisers of such investors`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "regard must be had to (a) the nature of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts and the nature of the entity concerned; (b) the matters that likely investors may reasonably be expected to know; and (c) the fact that certain matters may reasonably be expected to be known to the professional advisers of such investors"

-- s 243(4A): incorporation by reference. A power limited by its own wording ("Subject to any condition or restriction ... prescribed"; lodged "together with the prospectus"): NOTHING outside it.
-- src:39984 | (4A) Subject to any condition or restriction as may be prescribed by
-- src:39985 | regulations made under section 341, the information mentioned in
-- src:39986 | subsection (1) may be incorporated in the prospectus by reference to a
-- src:39987 | document (called in this subsection and subsection (4B) the reference
-- src:39988 | document) lodged with the Authority together with the prospectus.
@ref s 243(4A) (src:39984-39988)
GIVEN
    `the reference document is lodged with the Authority together with the prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document you refer to lodged with the Authority together with the prospectus?
    `every condition or restriction prescribed by regulations made under section 341 is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is every condition or restriction prescribed by regulations made under section 341 for incorporation by reference met (answer yes if none is prescribed)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(4A) the information may be incorporated in the prospectus by reference to the reference document` MEANS
    IF `the reference document is lodged with the Authority together with the prospectus` AND `every condition or restriction prescribed by regulations made under section 341 is met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to any condition or restriction as may be prescribed by regulations made under section 341, the information mentioned in subsection (1) may be incorporated in the prospectus by reference to a document (called in this subsection and subsection (4B) the reference document) lodged with the Authority together with the prospectus"

-- s 243(4B): the information in the reference document is part of the prospectus.
-- src:39992 | (4B) For the purposes of this Division, the information contained in
-- src:39993 | the reference document is to be regarded as part of the prospectus.
@ref s 243(4B) (src:39992-39993)
GIVEN
    `the information is contained in the reference document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information contained in the reference document referred to in section 243(4A)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(4B) the information is part of the prospectus` MEANS
    IF `the information is contained in the reference document`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the information contained in the reference document is to be regarded as part of the prospectus"

-- s 243(5): whose knowledge is relevant. "only if" closes the list.
-- src:39997 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (2)(b), a person’s knowledge is
-- src:39998 | relevant only if the person is one of the following:
-- src:40000 | (a) the person making the offer;
-- src:40005 | (b) if the person making the offer is an entity, a director or an
