-- src:40020 | (f) a person named in the prospectus with the person’s consent
-- src:40021 | as having made a statement —
-- src:40023 | (i) that is included in the prospectus; or
-- src:40025 | (ii) on which a statement made in the prospectus is
-- src:40026 | based;
-- src:40028 | (g) a person named in the prospectus with the person’s consent
-- src:40029 | as having performed a particular professional or advisory
-- src:40030 | function.
@ref s 243(5) (src:39997-40030)
GIVEN
    `the person is the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the person making the offer?
    `the person making the offer is an entity and the person is a director or an equivalent person of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person making the offer an entity, and is the person a director or an equivalent person of the entity?
    `the person is the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person the issuer?
    `the person is a director or an equivalent person, or a proposed director or an equivalent person, of the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a director or an equivalent person, or a proposed director or an equivalent person, of the issuer?
    `the person is named in the prospectus with the person's consent as an underwriter to the issue or sale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person named in the prospectus, with the person's consent, as an underwriter to the issue or sale?
    `the person is named in the prospectus as a stockbroker to the issue or sale and participates in any way in the preparation of the prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person named in the prospectus as a stockbroker to the issue or sale, and does the person participate in any way in the preparation of the prospectus?
    `the person is named in the prospectus with the person's consent as having made a statement that is included in the prospectus or on which a statement made in the prospectus is based` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person named in the prospectus, with the person's consent, as having made a statement that is included in the prospectus, or on which a statement made in the prospectus is based?
    `the person is named in the prospectus with the person's consent as having performed a particular professional or advisory function` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person named in the prospectus, with the person's consent, as having performed a particular professional or advisory function?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(5) the person's knowledge is relevant` MEANS
    IF `the person is the person making the offer` OR `the person making the offer is an entity and the person is a director or an equivalent person of the entity` OR `the person is the issuer` OR `the person is a director or an equivalent person, or a proposed director or an equivalent person, of the issuer` OR `the person is named in the prospectus with the person's consent as an underwriter to the issue or sale` OR `the person is named in the prospectus as a stockbroker to the issue or sale and participates in any way in the preparation of the prospectus` OR `the person is named in the prospectus with the person's consent as having made a statement that is included in the prospectus or on which a statement made in the prospectus is based` OR `the person is named in the prospectus with the person's consent as having performed a particular professional or advisory function`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person's knowledge is relevant only if the person is one of the following"

-- s 243(6): a condition that waives compliance, or affects the applicant with notice, is void.
-- src:40032 | (6) A condition requiring or binding an applicant for securities or
-- src:40033 | securities‑based derivatives contracts to waive compliance with any
-- src:40034 | requirement of this section, or purporting to affect the applicant with
-- src:40035 | notice of any contract, document or matter not specifically referred to
-- src:40036 | in the prospectus, is void.
@ref s 243(6) (src:40032-40036)
GIVEN
    `the condition requires or binds an applicant to waive compliance with a requirement of this section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the condition require or bind an applicant for securities or securities-based derivatives contracts to waive compliance with a requirement of section 243?
    `the condition purports to affect the applicant with notice of a contract, document or matter not specifically referred to in the prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the condition purport to affect the applicant with notice of any contract, document or matter not specifically referred to in the prospectus?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(6) the condition is void` MEANS
    IF `the condition requires or binds an applicant to waive compliance with a requirement of this section` OR `the condition purports to affect the applicant with notice of a contract, document or matter not specifically referred to in the prospectus`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A condition requiring or binding an applicant ... to waive compliance with any requirement of this section, or purporting to affect the applicant with notice of any contract, document or matter not specifically referred to in the prospectus, is void" names the conditions and says nothing of any other

-- s 243(7): this section does not affect any liability under any other law.
-- src:40040 | (7) This section does not affect any liability that a person has under
-- src:40041 | any other law.
@ref s 243(7) (src:40040-40041)
GIVEN
    `the liability arises under another law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the liability one that the person has under another law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(7) this section affects the liability` MEANS
    IF `the liability arises under another law`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not affect any liability that a person has under any other law"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative names a liability under another law and says nothing of any other

-- s 243(8): two terms defined for business trusts in subsection (3)(e).
-- src:40043 | (8) In subsection (3)(e) —
-- src:40045 | “assets and liabilities, profits and losses, financial position and
-- src:40046 | performance”, in relation to a business trust, means the assets
-- src:40047 | and liabilities, profits and losses, financial position and
-- src:40048 | performance of that business trust derived from the
-- src:40049 | accounting records and other records kept by the
-- src:40050 | trustee‑manager of that business trust;
@ref s 243(8) "assets and liabilities, profits and losses, financial position and performance" (src:40043-40050)
GIVEN
    `the term is used in subsection (3)(e) in relation to a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the term used, in section 243(3)(e), in relation to a business trust?
    `the figures are derived from the accounting records and other records kept by the trustee-manager of the business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the figures derived from the accounting records and other records kept by the trustee-manager of the business trust?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(8) "assets and liabilities, profits and losses, financial position and performance" the figures are those of the business trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the term is used in subsection (3)(e) in relation to a business trust`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In subsection (3)(e) ... in relation to a business trust, means"
        IF `the figures are derived from the accounting records and other records kept by the trustee-manager of the business trust`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a business trust, means the assets and liabilities, profits and losses, financial position and performance of that business trust derived from the accounting records and other records kept by the trustee-manager of that business trust"

-- src:40055 | “prospects”, in relation to a business trust, means the business
-- src:40056 | and financial prospects anticipated with respect to the
-- src:40057 | operations of the trustee‑manager of the business trust, in
-- src:40058 | its capacity as trustee‑manager of the business trust.
@ref s 243(8) "prospects" (src:40055-40058)
GIVEN
    `the term is used in subsection (3)(e) in relation to a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the term used, in section 243(3)(e), in relation to a business trust?
    `the prospects are the business and financial prospects anticipated with respect to the operations of the trustee-manager in its capacity as trustee-manager` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the prospects the business and financial prospects anticipated with respect to the operations of the trustee-manager of the business trust, in its capacity as trustee-manager?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(8) "prospects" the prospects are those of the business trust` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the term is used in subsection (3)(e) in relation to a business trust`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In subsection (3)(e) ... in relation to a business trust, means"
        IF `the prospects are the business and financial prospects anticipated with respect to the operations of the trustee-manager in its capacity as trustee-manager`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to a business trust, means the business and financial prospects anticipated with respect to the operations of the trustee-manager of the business trust, in its capacity as trustee-manager of the business trust"

§ `s 245: over-subscriptions and asset-backing in debenture issues`

-- s 245(1): the entity must not accept or retain over-subscriptions unless the prospectus reserves the right and states a limit of not more than 25%. "unless" is a closed gate.
-- src:40067 | 245.—(1) An entity must not accept or retain subscriptions to a
-- src:40068 | debenture issue in excess of the amount of the issue as disclosed in the
-- src:40069 | prospectus unless the entity has specified in the prospectus —
-- src:40071 | (a) that it expressly reserves the right to accept or retain
-- src:40072 | over‑subscriptions; and
-- src:40074 | (b) a limit expressed as a specific sum of money on the amount
-- src:40075 | of over‑subscriptions that may be accepted or retained,
-- src:40076 | being an amount not more than 25% in excess of the
-- src:40077 | amount of the issue as disclosed in the prospectus.
@ref s 245(1) (src:40067-40077)
GIVEN
    `the body is an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body an entity (as section 2(1) defines "entity")?
    `the entity accepts or retains subscriptions to a debenture issue in excess of the amount of the issue disclosed in the prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you accept or retain subscriptions to a debenture issue in excess of the amount of the issue as disclosed in the prospectus?
    `the prospectus expressly reserves the right to accept or retain over-subscriptions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus say that you expressly reserve the right to accept or retain over-subscriptions?
    `the prospectus states a limit on the over-subscriptions that may be accepted or retained, expressed as a specific sum of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus state a limit, expressed as a specific sum of money, on the amount of over-subscriptions that may be accepted or retained?
    `the amount of the issue as disclosed in the prospectus` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the issue, as disclosed in the prospectus, in dollars?
    `the limit on the over-subscriptions stated in the prospectus` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the limit on over-subscriptions stated in the prospectus, in dollars (0 if none is stated)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F27 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 245(1) the entity must not accept or retain the subscriptions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the body is an entity`) OR (NOT `the entity accepts or retains subscriptions to a debenture issue in excess of the amount of the issue disclosed in the prospectus`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An entity must not accept or retain subscriptions to a debenture issue in excess of the amount of the issue as disclosed in the prospectus"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        IF `the prospectus expressly reserves the right to accept or retain over-subscriptions` AND `the prospectus states a limit on the over-subscriptions that may be accepted or retained, expressed as a specific sum of money` AND (`the limit on the over-subscriptions stated in the prospectus` AT MOST ((`the amount of the issue as disclosed in the prospectus` TIMES 25) DIVIDED BY 100))
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the entity has specified in the prospectus (a) that it expressly reserves the right to accept or retain over-subscriptions; and (b) a limit expressed as a specific sum of money on the amount of over-subscriptions that may be accepted or retained, being an amount not more than 25% in excess of the amount of the issue as disclosed in the prospectus"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 245(1) (the prohibition as a rule) (src:40067-40077)
GIVEN
    `the entity` IS A Party @desc Who is the entity that accepts or retains the subscriptions?
    `what section 245(1) answers for the entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 245(1) the entity must not accept or retain the subscriptions` answer for the entity? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 243 action`
`s 245(1) the entity shall not accept or retain over-subscriptions` MEANS
    IF `what section 245(1) answers for the entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the entity`
         SHANT `s 245(1) accept or retain subscriptions in excess of the amount of the issue`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the entity` BECAUSE "subscriptions were accepted or retained in excess of the amount of the issue disclosed in the prospectus without the reservation and limit section 245(1) requires; section 245(3) makes that an offence"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 245(2)(a): once the entity reserves the right to accept or retain over-subscriptions, it must not make, authorise or permit a statement of asset-backing other than the total tangible assets and total liabilities of the entity and its guarantors. "Subject to regulations" is taken as an input (the text points outside itself).
-- src:40079 | (2) Subject to regulations made by the Authority for the purposes of
-- src:40080 | this subsection, where an entity specifies in a prospectus relating to a
-- src:40081 | debenture issue that it reserves the right to accept or retain
-- src:40082 | over‑subscriptions —
-- src:40084 | (a) the entity must not make, authorise or permit any statement
-- src:40085 | of or reference as to the asset‑backing for the issue to be
-- src:40086 | made or contained in any prospectus relating to the issue,
-- src:40087 | other than a statement or reference to the total tangible
-- src:40088 | assets and the total liabilities of the entity and of its
-- src:40089 | guarantor entities; and
@ref s 245(2)(a) (src:40079-40089)
GIVEN
    `regulations made by the Authority for the purposes of subsection (2) apply to the case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do regulations made by the Authority for the purposes of section 245(2) apply to the case?
    `the entity specifies in a prospectus relating to a debenture issue that it reserves the right to accept or retain over-subscriptions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus relating to the debenture issue specify that you reserve the right to accept or retain over-subscriptions?
    `the entity makes, authorises or permits a statement of or reference as to the asset-backing for the issue to be made or contained in a prospectus relating to the issue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make, authorise or permit any statement of, or reference as to, the asset-backing for the issue to be made or contained in a prospectus relating to the issue?
    `the statement or reference is only to the total tangible assets and the total liabilities of the entity and of its guarantor entities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the statement or reference only to the total tangible assets and the total liabilities of the entity and of its guarantor entities?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F28 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 245(2)(a) the entity must not make, authorise or permit the statement of asset-backing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `regulations made by the Authority for the purposes of subsection (2) apply to the case`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to regulations made by the Authority for the purposes of this subsection"
        IF (NOT `the entity specifies in a prospectus relating to a debenture issue that it reserves the right to accept or retain over-subscriptions`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an entity specifies in a prospectus relating to a debenture issue that it reserves the right to accept or retain over-subscriptions"
        IF (NOT `the entity makes, authorises or permits a statement of or reference as to the asset-backing for the issue to be made or contained in a prospectus relating to the issue`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the entity must not make, authorise or permit any statement of or reference as to the asset-backing for the issue to be made or contained in any prospectus relating to the issue"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        IF `the statement or reference is only to the total tangible assets and the total liabilities of the entity and of its guarantor entities`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than a statement or reference to the total tangible assets and the total liabilities of the entity and of its guarantor entities"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 245(2)(a) (the prohibition as a rule) (src:40079-40089)
GIVEN
    `the entity` IS A Party @desc Who is the entity that makes, authorises or permits the statement?
    `what section 245(2)(a) answers for the entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 245(2)(a) the entity must not make, authorise or permit the statement of asset-backing` answer for the entity? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 243 action`
`s 245(2)(a) the entity shall not make, authorise or permit a statement of asset-backing` MEANS
    IF `what section 245(2)(a) answers for the entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the entity`
         SHANT `s 245(2) make, authorise or permit a statement of the asset-backing`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the entity` BECAUSE "a statement of the asset-backing for the issue was made, authorised or permitted; section 245(3) makes that an offence"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 245(2)(b): the prospectus must contain a statement of what the totals would be if over-subscriptions to the limit were accepted. A duty with a "where" gate: NOTHING when it is unmet (fork F18).
-- src:40091 | (b) the prospectus must contain a statement or reference as to
-- src:40092 | what the total assets and total liabilities of the entity would
-- src:40093 | be if over‑subscriptions to the limit specified in the
-- src:40094 | prospectus were accepted or retained.
@ref s 245(2)(b) (src:40091-40094)
GIVEN
    `the entity specifies in a prospectus relating to a debenture issue that it reserves the right to accept or retain over-subscriptions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus relating to the debenture issue specify that you reserve the right to accept or retain over-subscriptions?
    `the prospectus contains a statement or reference as to what the total assets and total liabilities of the entity would be if over-subscriptions to the limit specified were accepted or retained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus contain a statement or reference as to what the total assets and total liabilities of the entity would be if over-subscriptions to the limit specified in the prospectus were accepted or retained?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 245(2)(b) the prospectus contains the statement of total assets and total liabilities` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the entity specifies in a prospectus relating to a debenture issue that it reserves the right to accept or retain over-subscriptions`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where an entity specifies in a prospectus relating to a debenture issue that it reserves the right to accept or retain over-subscriptions"
        IF `the prospectus contains a statement or reference as to what the total assets and total liabilities of the entity would be if over-subscriptions to the limit specified were accepted or retained`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the prospectus must contain a statement or reference as to what the total assets and total liabilities of the entity would be if over-subscriptions to the limit specified in the prospectus were accepted or retained"

-- s 245(3): the offence of contravening (1) or (2), and its penalty.
-- src:40096 | (3) Every entity or other person that contravenes subsection (1) or
-- src:40097 | (2) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a
-- src:40098 | fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to
-- src:40103 | a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day
-- src:40104 | during which the offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 245(3) (src:40096-40104)
GIVEN
    `what section 245(1) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 245(1) the entity must not accept or retain the subscriptions` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 245(2)(a) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 245(2)(a) the entity must not make, authorise or permit the statement of asset-backing` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `what section 245(2)(b) answers for the person` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 245(2)(b) the prospectus contains the statement of total assets and total liabilities` answer for the person? (JUST TRUE if the statement is there, JUST FALSE if it is not, NOTHING if no duty arises.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F29 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 245(3) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`what section 245(1) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 245(2)(a) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 245(2)(b) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`what section 245(1) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`what section 245(2)(a) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND ((`what section 245(2)(b) answers for the person` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`what section 245(2)(b) answers for the person` EQUALS NOTHING))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every entity or other person that contravenes subsection (1) or (2) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an answer under subsection (1) or (2) was not worked out, or the person contravenes neither

@ref s 245(3) (the penalty) (src:40096-40104)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 245(3) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000  -- a fine not exceeding $50,000; no imprisonment is stated (0); a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

§ `s 246: what a profile statement must contain`

-- s 246(1): the profile statement contains the particulars (a), the statement (b) and the statement (c). Paragraphs (ia) and (ib) apply only where their case arises.
-- src:40108 | 246.—(1) A profile statement for an offer of securities or
-- src:40109 | securities‑based derivatives contracts must contain —
-- src:40111 | (a) the following particulars:
-- src:40113 | (i) identification of the person making the offer;
-- src:40115 | (ia) where the person making the offer is not the issuer,
-- src:40116 | identification of the issuer and, where applicable, the
-- src:40117 | underlying entity;
-- src:40119 | (ib) in the case of an offer of securities or securities‑based
-- src:40120 | derivatives contracts being units or derivatives of
-- src:40121 | units in a business trust, identification of the business
-- src:40122 | trust, the trustee‑manager of the business trust and
-- src:40123 | the issuer;
-- src:40125 | (ii) identification of the persons signing the profile
-- src:40126 | statement;
-- src:40128 | (iii) the nature of the securities or securities‑based
-- src:40129 | derivatives contracts;
-- src:40131 | (iv) the nature of the risks involved in investing in the
-- src:40132 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts;
-- src:40134 | (v) details of all amounts payable in respect of the
-- src:40135 | securities or securities‑based derivatives contracts
-- src:40136 | (including any amount by way of fee, commission or
-- src:40137 | charge);
-- src:40139 | (b) a statement that copies of the prospectus are available for
-- src:40140 | collection at the times and places specified in the profile
-- src:40141 | statement; and
-- src:40143 | (c) a statement that the persons referred to in section 240(4A)
-- src:40144 | who have signed the profile statement are satisfied that the
-- src:40145 | profile statement contains a fair summary of the key
-- src:40146 | information in the prospectus.
@ref s 246(1) (src:40108-40146)
GIVEN
    `the document is a profile statement for an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a profile statement for an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `it identifies the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the profile statement identify the person making the offer?
    `the person making the offer is not the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person making the offer not the issuer?
    `it identifies the issuer and, where applicable, the underlying entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the profile statement identify the issuer and, where applicable, the underlying entity?
    `the offer is of units or derivatives of units in a business trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer of units or derivatives of units in a business trust?
    `it identifies the business trust, the trustee-manager of the business trust and the issuer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the profile statement identify the business trust, the trustee-manager of the business trust and the issuer?
    `it identifies the persons signing the profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the profile statement identify the persons signing it?
    `it states the nature of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the profile statement state the nature of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `it states the nature of the risks involved in investing in the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the profile statement state the nature of the risks involved in investing in the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts?
    `it gives details of all amounts payable in respect of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, including any amount by way of fee, commission or charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the profile statement give details of all amounts payable in respect of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, including any amount by way of fee, commission or charge?
    `it states that copies of the prospectus are available for collection at the times and places specified in the profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the profile statement state that copies of the prospectus are available for collection at the times and places specified in it?
    `it states that the persons referred to in section 240(4A) who have signed are satisfied that it contains a fair summary of the key information in the prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the profile statement state that the persons referred to in section 240(4A) who have signed it are satisfied that it contains a fair summary of the key information in the prospectus?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 246(1) the profile statement contains what it must contain` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the document is a profile statement for an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A profile statement for an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts must contain"
        IF `it identifies the person making the offer` AND ((NOT `the person making the offer is not the issuer`) OR `it identifies the issuer and, where applicable, the underlying entity`) AND ((NOT `the offer is of units or derivatives of units in a business trust`) OR `it identifies the business trust, the trustee-manager of the business trust and the issuer`) AND `it identifies the persons signing the profile statement` AND `it states the nature of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` AND `it states the nature of the risks involved in investing in the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts` AND `it gives details of all amounts payable in respect of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts, including any amount by way of fee, commission or charge` AND `it states that copies of the prospectus are available for collection at the times and places specified in the profile statement` AND `it states that the persons referred to in section 240(4A) who have signed are satisfied that it contains a fair summary of the key information in the prospectus`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A profile statement for an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts must contain (a) the following particulars: (i) identification of the person making the offer; (ia) where the person making the offer is not the issuer, identification of the issuer and, where applicable, the underlying entity; (ib) in the case of an offer of securities or securities-based derivatives contracts being units or derivatives of units in a business trust, identification of the business trust, the trustee-manager of the business trust and the issuer; (ii) identification of the persons signing the profile statement; (iii) the nature of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts; (iv) the nature of the risks involved in investing in the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts; (v) details of all amounts payable in respect of the securities or securities-based derivatives contracts (including any amount by way of fee, commission or charge); (b) a statement that copies of the prospectus are available for collection at the times and places specified in the profile statement; and (c) a statement that the persons referred to in section 240(4A) who have signed the profile statement are satisfied that the profile statement contains a fair summary of the key information in the prospectus"

-- s 246(2): what a profile statement must not contain. The prohibited things are the three limbs; a statement with none of them is outside the bar (SPLIT-SITE (i)).
-- src:40153 | (2) A profile statement must not contain —
-- src:40155 | (a) any statement that is false or misleading in the form and
-- src:40156 | context in which it is included;
-- src:40158 | (b) any material information that is not contained in the
-- src:40159 | prospectus; and
-- src:40161 | (c) any material information that differs in any material
-- src:40162 | particular from that set out in the prospectus.
@ref s 246(2) (src:40153-40162)
GIVEN
    `the document is a profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document a profile statement?
    `it contains a statement that is false or misleading in the form and context in which it is included` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the profile statement contain a statement that is false or misleading in the form and context in which it is included?
    `it contains material information that is not contained in the prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the profile statement contain any material information that is not contained in the prospectus?
    `it contains material information that differs in a material particular from that set out in the prospectus` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the profile statement contain any material information that differs in any material particular from that set out in the prospectus?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F30 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 246(2) the profile statement contains something it must not contain` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the document is a profile statement`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A profile statement must not contain"
        IF `it contains a statement that is false or misleading in the form and context in which it is included` OR `it contains material information that is not contained in the prospectus` OR `it contains material information that differs in a material particular from that set out in the prospectus`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A profile statement must not contain (a) any statement that is false or misleading in the form and context in which it is included; (b) any material information that is not contained in the prospectus; and (c) any material information that differs in any material particular from that set out in the prospectus"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)

-- s 246(3): the reference to a statement in subsection (2)(a) includes information presented in any form.
-- src:40164 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2)(a), the reference to a
-- src:40165 | statement includes a reference to any information presented,
-- src:40166 | regardless of whether such information is in text or otherwise.
@ref s 246(3) (src:40164-40166)
GIVEN
    `the information is presented, whether in text or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the information presented in the profile statement, whether in text or otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 246(3) the information presented is a statement for the purposes of subsection (2)(a)` MEANS
    IF `the information is presented, whether in text or otherwise`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the reference to a statement includes a reference to any information presented" lists without closing the list

§ `s 247: exemption from the requirements as to form or content`

-- s 247(1) and (3): the Authority's exemption of a person, a class, a prospectus or a profile statement from a requirement of form or content. The text says when the Authority may exempt and says nothing of a person it has not exempted.
-- src:40171 | 247.—(1) The Authority may exempt any person or any prospectus
-- src:40172 | or profile statement from any requirement of this Act relating to the
-- src:40173 | form or content of a prospectus or profile statement, subject to such
-- src:40174 | conditions or restrictions as the Authority may determine.
@ref s 247(1) (src:40171-40174)
-- src:40187 | (3) The Authority may exempt any class of persons, or any class or
-- src:40188 | description of prospectuses or profile statements, from any
-- src:40189 | requirement of this Act relating to the form or content of a
-- src:40190 | prospectus or profile statement, subject to such conditions or
-- src:40191 | restrictions as the Authority may determine.
@ref s 247(3) (src:40187-40191)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has exempted the person, the prospectus or profile statement, or a class to which it belongs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority exempted you, or the prospectus or profile statement, or a class of persons or of prospectuses or profile statements to which it belongs, from a requirement of the Act relating to the form or content of a prospectus or profile statement?
    `the exemption extends to the requirement asked about` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the exemption extend to the requirement you ask about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 247(1) and (3) the person or document is exempt from the requirement of form or content` MEANS
    IF `the Authority has exempted the person, the prospectus or profile statement, or a class to which it belongs` AND `the exemption extends to the requirement asked about`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Authority may exempt any person or any prospectus or profile statement from any requirement of this Act relating to the form or content of a prospectus or profile statement"

-- s 247(2): the Authority must not grant an exemption under (1) unless it is of one of two opinions. "unless" closes the bar.
-- src:40176 | (2) The Authority must not grant an exemption under subsection (1)
-- src:40177 | unless it is of the opinion that —
-- src:40179 | (a) the cost of complying with the requirement in respect of
-- src:40180 | which exemption has been applied for outweighs the
-- src:40181 | resulting protection to investors; or
-- src:40183 | (b) it would not be prejudicial to the public interest if the
-- src:40184 | requirement in respect of which exemption has been
-- src:40185 | applied for were dispensed with.
@ref s 247(2) (src:40176-40185)
GIVEN
    `the Authority is of the opinion that the cost of complying with the requirement outweighs the resulting protection to investors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority of the opinion that the cost of complying with the requirement in respect of which exemption has been applied for outweighs the resulting protection to investors?
    `the Authority is of the opinion that it would not be prejudicial to the public interest to dispense with the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority of the opinion that it would not be prejudicial to the public interest if the requirement in respect of which exemption has been applied for were dispensed with?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 247(2) the Authority is barred from granting the exemption under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the Authority is of the opinion that the cost of complying with the requirement outweighs the resulting protection to investors` OR `the Authority is of the opinion that it would not be prejudicial to the public interest to dispense with the requirement`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Authority must not grant an exemption under subsection (1) unless it is of the opinion that (a) the cost of complying with the requirement in respect of which exemption has been applied for outweighs the resulting protection to investors; or (b) it would not be prejudicial to the public interest if the requirement in respect of which exemption has been applied for were dispensed with"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 247(5): the offence of contravening a condition or restriction, and its penalty.
-- src:40195 | (5) Any person who contravenes any of the conditions or
-- src:40196 | restrictions imposed under subsection (1) or (3) shall be guilty of
-- src:40197 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:40202 | $50,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:40203 | exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day during which the
-- src:40204 | offence continues after conviction.
@ref s 247(5) (src:40195-40204)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you contravene a condition or restriction imposed under section 247(1) or (3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F31 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 247(5) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes a condition or restriction imposed under subsection (1) or (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person who contravenes any of the conditions or restrictions imposed under subsection (1) or (3) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)

@ref s 247(5) (the penalty) (src:40195-40204)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 247(5) the penalty for the offence` MEANS
    Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000  -- a fine not exceeding $50,000; no imprisonment is stated (0); a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day the offence continues after conviction

@ref s 247(5) (the prohibition on contravening a condition) (src:40195-40204)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party @desc Who is bound by the condition or restriction?
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 243 action`
`s 247(5) the person shall not contravene a condition or restriction` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    SHANT `s 247(5) contravene the condition or restriction`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "a condition or restriction imposed under section 247(1) or (3) was contravened, which is an offence under section 247(5)"

§ `s 248: governmental and international entities, signing of the copy`

-- s 248(1): the section applies only to entities that are both of a governmental and international character. "only" closes it.
-- src:40210 | 248.—(1) This section applies only to entities that are both of a
-- src:40211 | governmental and international character.
@ref s 248(1) (src:40210-40211)
GIVEN
    `the entity is of a governmental character` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity of a governmental character?
    `the entity is of an international character` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the entity of an international character?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 248(1) this section applies to the entity` MEANS
    IF `the entity is of a governmental character` AND `the entity is of an international character`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies only to entities that are both of a governmental and international character"

-- s 248(2): the entity may apply in writing; the Authority may, if it considers the requirements unduly burdensome, exempt the entity.
-- src:40213 | (2) An entity to which this section applies may apply in writing to
-- src:40214 | the Authority for an exemption from the requirements of
-- src:40215 | section 240(1)(a)(ii), (4)(b), (4A), (13)(c) and (14)(c) and the
-- src:40216 | Authority may, if it considers those requirements unduly
-- src:40217 | burdensome on the entity, exempt such entity from complying
-- src:40218 | therewith.
@ref s 248(2) (src:40213-40218)
GIVEN
    `this section applies to the entity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function `s 248(1) this section applies to the entity` answer for the entity? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if you do not know.)
    `the entity has applied in writing to the Authority for an exemption from the requirements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the entity applied in writing to the Authority for an exemption from the requirements of section 240(1)(a)(ii), (4)(b), (4A), (13)(c) and (14)(c)?
    `the Authority considers those requirements unduly burdensome on the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Authority consider those requirements unduly burdensome on the entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F32 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 248(2) the Authority may exempt the entity from the requirements` MEANS
    IF (`this section applies to the entity` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the entity has applied in writing to the Authority for an exemption from the requirements` AND `the Authority considers those requirements unduly burdensome on the entity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An entity to which this section applies may apply in writing to the Authority for an exemption from the requirements of section 240(1)(a)(ii), (4)(b), (4A), (13)(c) and (14)(c) and the Authority may, if it considers those requirements unduly burdensome on the entity, exempt such entity from complying therewith"  -- GRANT-RULING (1): an "if" gate failed on a function named for a power; the other reading is JUST FALSE

-- s 248(3): the Authority may subject the exemption to a minimum number of directors resident in Singapore who must sign.
-- src:40220 | (3) The Authority may subject such exemption to a requirement
-- src:40221 | that such minimum number of directors or equivalent persons who
-- src:40222 | are resident in Singapore as the Authority may, in that case, decide
-- src:40223 | must sign the copy of the prospectus or profile statement.
@ref s 248(3) (src:40220-40223)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has subjected the exemption to a requirement that a minimum number of directors or equivalent persons resident in Singapore must sign` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority subjected the exemption to a requirement that a minimum number of directors or equivalent persons who are resident in Singapore must sign the copy?
    `the number of directors or equivalent persons resident in Singapore who have signed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many directors or equivalent persons who are resident in Singapore have signed the copy?
    `the minimum number the Authority has decided` IS A NUMBER @desc What minimum number of directors or equivalent persons resident in Singapore has the Authority decided must sign?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 248(3) the requirement as to signing by directors resident in Singapore is met` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the Authority has subjected the exemption to a requirement that a minimum number of directors or equivalent persons resident in Singapore must sign`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Authority may subject such exemption to a requirement that such minimum number of directors or equivalent persons who are resident in Singapore as the Authority may, in that case, decide must sign"
        IF `the number of directors or equivalent persons resident in Singapore who have signed` AT LEAST `the minimum number the Authority has decided`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "such minimum number of directors or equivalent persons who are resident in Singapore as the Authority may, in that case, decide must sign the copy of the prospectus or profile statement"

-- s 248(4): where no director is resident in Singapore, a duly authorised agent may sign, so long as the authorisation is supported by a board resolution. "so long as" closes the grant.
-- src:40225 | (4) In the event that no director or equivalent person is resident in
-- src:40226 | Singapore, the Authority may permit a duly authorised agent to sign
-- src:40227 | the prospectus or profile statement so long as such authorisation is
-- src:40228 | supported by a resolution of the board of the entity.
@ref s 248(4) (src:40225-40228)
GIVEN
    `no director or equivalent person is resident in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is no director or equivalent person of the entity resident in Singapore?
    `the authorisation is supported by a resolution of the board of the entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the authorisation of the agent supported by a resolution of the board of the entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F32 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 248(4) the Authority may permit a duly authorised agent to sign` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `no director or equivalent person is resident in Singapore`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In the event that no director or equivalent person is resident in Singapore, the Authority may permit a duly authorised agent to sign the prospectus or profile statement"  -- GRANT-RULING (1): an "if" gate failed on a function named for a power; the other reading is JUST FALSE
        IF (NOT `the authorisation is supported by a resolution of the board of the entity`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "so long as such authorisation is supported by a resolution of the board of the entity"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 248(5): the Authority may grant the exemption applied for if satisfied that the entity cannot comply with (3) or (4).
-- src:40230 | (5) The Authority may, if satisfied that a particular entity cannot
-- src:40231 | comply with any of the requirements in subsection (3) or (4), grant the
-- src:40232 | exemption applied for.
@ref s 248(5) (src:40230-40232)
GIVEN
    `the Authority is satisfied that the entity cannot comply with a requirement in subsection (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority satisfied that the entity cannot comply with any of the requirements in section 248(3) or (4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FORK F32 (see NOTES.md, Fork register)
`s 248(5) the Authority may grant the exemption applied for` MEANS
    IF `the Authority is satisfied that the entity cannot comply with a requirement in subsection (3) or (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Authority may, if satisfied that a particular entity cannot comply with any of the requirements in subsection (3) or (4), grant the exemption applied for"  -- GRANT-RULING (1): an "if" gate failed on a function named for a power; the other reading is JUST FALSE

-- s 248(6): a prospectus or profile statement that complies with the terms of the exemption is deemed a prospectus or profile statement, and the Authority must register a copy.
-- src:40234 | (6) Any prospectus or profile statement that complies with the
-- src:40235 | terms of exemption granted by the Authority is deemed to be a
-- src:40236 | prospectus or profile statement for the purposes of this Division and a
-- src:40237 | copy of such prospectus or profile statement must be registered by the
-- src:40238 | Authority.
@ref s 248(6) (src:40234-40238)
GIVEN
    `the prospectus or profile statement complies with the terms of the exemption granted by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus or profile statement comply with the terms of the exemption granted by the Authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 248(6) the document is deemed to be a prospectus or profile statement for the purposes of this Division` MEANS
    IF `the prospectus or profile statement complies with the terms of the exemption granted by the Authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any prospectus or profile statement that complies with the terms of exemption granted by the Authority is deemed to be a prospectus or profile statement for the purposes of this Division"

@ref s 248(6) (the registration) (src:40234-40238)
GIVEN
    `the prospectus or profile statement complies with the terms of the exemption granted by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the prospectus or profile statement comply with the terms of the exemption granted by the Authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 248(6) a copy of the document must be registered by the Authority` MEANS
    IF `the prospectus or profile statement complies with the terms of the exemption granted by the Authority`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a copy of such prospectus or profile statement must be registered by the Authority" reaches a document that complies with the terms of the exemption
